                        ],
                        "form": "die Huftiere"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "37df3042-738a-3fe5-9ebe-bdb66b0c26a9",
                        "entry_id": "311d1e93-be98-3962-b470-3991f4c7aed8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Mitglied einer großen Gruppe von Säugetieren, die auf den Zehenspitzen gehen und bei denen typischerweise die Nägel zu Hufen umgebildet sind"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "533c859a-82bc-4ba3-be05-8ca5f03fa107",
                                "sense_id": "37df3042-738a-3fe5-9ebe-bdb66b0c26a9",
                                "text": "Im Zoo wurde eine neue Pflegerin für die Huftiere eingestellt."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8b5c620d-bd0b-497e-9d4e-e133d6a8df02",
                                "sense_id": "37df3042-738a-3fe5-9ebe-bdb66b0c26a9",
                                "text": "„Huftiere sind insgesamt meistens eher nicht so gut mit Stufen, daher war das sicher eine ziemliche Quälerei.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "06af862d-600a-46fe-990c-66178f7b6fcc",
                        "source_entry_id": "311d1e93-be98-3962-b470-3991f4c7aed8",
                        "source_sense_id": "37df3042-738a-3fe5-9ebe-bdb66b0c26a9",
                        "source_sense_description": "Tier mit Hufen",
                        "target_lang_word": "ungulate",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ungulate",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1af26b80-6a41-39d5-ac98-2f738d1448fb",
                                        "entry_id": "aa1fd4c9-837a-3703-b315-0aa1198558e0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having hooves."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4191b3c9-c11d-44cc-873c-f3dce3765451",
                                                "sense_id": "1af26b80-6a41-39d5-ac98-2f738d1448fb",
                                                "text": "When Owen wrote his description there was no evidence to determine the character of the extremities, whether they were ungulate, unguiculate, or pinnate, while the structure of the nostrils suggested"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f0bcfd8d-fe68-4be6-a121-d9a0bd8a58ba",
                                                "sense_id": "1af26b80-6a41-39d5-ac98-2f738d1448fb",
                                                "text": "Unlike the serial manus and pes of the edentata the carpus and tarsus are here diplarthrous in structure or displaced upon each other. While the Condylarthra are ungulate with an unguiculate carpus and tarsus, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e05c5398-d975-4161-8ac2-a07c915411d3",
                                                "sense_id": "1af26b80-6a41-39d5-ac98-2f738d1448fb",
                                                "text": "Like nearly all the land animals of Jupiter, as I was to learn later, they were ungulate, hoofs evidently being rendered necessary by the considerable areas of hardened lava on the surface of the planet, […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "db07f0d3-dee3-342f-8832-9c094e8b30ab",
                                        "entry_id": "aa1fd4c9-837a-3703-b315-0aa1198558e0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Shaped like a hoof."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "272358b4-da27-410b-b64c-2a4c4c3ee462",
                                                "sense_id": "db07f0d3-dee3-342f-8832-9c094e8b30ab",
                                                "text": "[…] areolet of only moderate size; first abscissa of the radius slightly more ungulate than in other varieties."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "ungulate",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bcf51ab1-f9a7-30a6-af59-1c9b00eb0392",
                                        "entry_id": "0f23450b-904e-3c6c-b444-4c04d4d54dd4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An ungulate animal; a hooved mammal."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a7a151af-34c7-41ef-ae7c-0cc4605a89e4",
                                                "sense_id": "bcf51ab1-f9a7-30a6-af59-1c9b00eb0392",
                                                "text": "The majority of large land mammals are ungulates."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6df60b2d-1edc-33a0-963c-238656749cac",
                                        "entry_id": "0f23450b-904e-3c6c-b444-4c04d4d54dd4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A member of the now obsolete clade Ungulata."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "especially"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "49b16a95-209d-4e76-983f-c7f88d52a9f5",
                        "source_entry_id": "311d1e93-be98-3962-b470-3991f4c7aed8",
                        "source_sense_id": "37df3042-738a-3fe5-9ebe-bdb66b0c26a9",
                        "source_sense_description": "Tier mit Hufen",
                        "target_lang_word": "ongulé",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ongulé",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e76d3db0-0f69-3d53-9151-7c8752ffe80d",
                                        "entry_id": "ee75f823-ce39-3f94-9f79-a003d65d2aac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Mammifère placentaire dont la dernière phalange du doigt ou des doigts est enveloppée d’un sabot."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "85c94578-6c14-45dc-8724-6487bcccf008",
                                                "sense_id": "e76d3db0-0f69-3d53-9151-7c8752ffe80d",
                                                "text": "Le mouflon de Corse : un ongulé casanier et cornu."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a9c9ad72-d31a-4e73-988a-878da12f4654",
                                                "sense_id": "e76d3db0-0f69-3d53-9151-7c8752ffe80d",
                                                "text": "Au cours du Tertiaire, les Ongulés ont transformé radicalement l’ajustement de leurs pattes ; les Carnassiers ont réduit et aiguisé leur denture."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f3131db4-0037-4533-aefd-0953a38de6c5",
                                                "sense_id": "e76d3db0-0f69-3d53-9151-7c8752ffe80d",
                                                "text": "Alors que les aigrettes se nourrissent essentiellement dans les milieux aquatiques, le garde-bœufs est une espèce grégaire terrestre qui vit en association étroite avec le bétail et les ongulés sauvages qu’il suit."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bc90def5-55a0-4703-bea8-ce4e105dd941",
                                                "sense_id": "e76d3db0-0f69-3d53-9151-7c8752ffe80d",
                                                "text": "On divise les ongulés en trois sous-ordres : les périssodactyles ou imparidigités, dont la patte se termine par un nombre impair de doigts [cinq, trois ou un seul], les porcins [quatre doigts par patte], enfin les ruminants [deux ou quatre doigts par patte] qui présentent de nombreuses particularités."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "ongulé",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d924c4f4-33c9-3873-8f77-a0521495ad73",
